{"title": "Show HN: TripCoral – Free itinerary and live updates from public flight data", "link": "https://www.tripcoral.com/", "summary": "<p>When TripCase shut down, I couldn't find an Android or web replacement I actually liked using. Especially with live flight tracking for gate and delay notifications.<p>So I built TripCoral. Airports and aviation authorities actually give out a lot of FIDS and air-traffic data for free: Avinor (Norway), Swedavia (Sweden), Schiphol (Netherlands), FAA SWIM (United States) etc. Instead of paying a commercial data broker, I wrote a Go collector that pulls from 100s of feeds covering ~1900 airports.<p>Forward your confirmation emails (flights, hotels, cars, dinner bookings) or enter a flight number, and it puts the whole trip on one timeline, works offline, and follows travel day live: check-in desks, gates, delays, security queues, indoor gate-to-gate walk times on tight connections, and baggage belts where published.<p>Google Play: <a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.tripcoral.app\">https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.tripcoral....</a><p>Web app: <a href=\"https://app.tripcoral.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://app.tripcoral.com</a><p>If you have a flight coming up, I'd love feedback on the UX or anything to make it more useful for travelers!</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50464273\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50464273</a></p>\n<p>Points: 1</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>", "published": "2026-11-12T07:55:25+00:00", "source": "Hacker News Best", "category": "techblog", "matched_entities": {}, "ontology": {"repo": "BlogRadar", "category": "techblog", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "source_event_model": "blog_post", "event_model_id": "tech.blog_post", "evidence_policy_ids": ["source_metadata", "article_text"], "event_model_payload": {"headline": "Show HN: TripCoral – Free itinerary and live updates from public flight data", "source_name": "Hacker News Best", "source_url": "https://www.tripcoral.com/", "published_at": "2026-11-12T07:55:25+00:00", "summary": "<p>When TripCase shut down, I couldn't find an Android or web replacement I actually liked using. Especially with live flight tracking for gate and delay notifications.<p>So I built TripCoral. Airports and aviation authorities actually give out a lot of FIDS and air-traffic data for free: Avinor (Norway), Swedavia (Sweden), Schiphol (Netherlands), FAA SWIM (United States) etc. Instead of paying a commercial data broker, I wrote a Go collector that pulls from 100s of feeds covering ~1900 airports.<p>Forward your confirmation emails (flights, hotels, cars, dinner bookings) or enter a flight number, and it puts the whole trip on one timeline, works offline, and follows travel day live: check-in desks, gates, delays, security queues, indoor gate-to-gate walk times on tight connections, and baggage belts where published.<p>Google Play: <a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.tripcoral.app\">https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.tripcoral....</a><p>Web app: <a href=\"https://app.tripcoral.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://app.tripcoral.com</a><p>If you have a flight coming up, I'd love feedback on the UX or anything to make it more useful for travelers!</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50464273\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50464273</a></p>\n<p>Points: 1</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>"}}, "logged_at": "2026-11-12T07:59:04.127755+00:00"}
