{"title": "Ask HN: Still Getting [Dead] Posts", "link": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50464172", "summary": "<p>Unfortunatelly, after quite some time, I'm still getting my posts flagged -- it's a technical blog post on my company's website, flagged as DoA.<p>Still unsure what am I doing wrong, I think the topic is relevant to HN and it's definitely not an ad - the system is a toy experiment to understand how the k8s control-plane works... (but running on a mac)</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50464172\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50464172</a></p>\n<p>Points: 2</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>", "published": "2026-11-12T07:39:52+00:00", "source": "Hacker News Best", "category": "techblog", "matched_entities": {}, "ontology": {"repo": "BlogRadar", "category": "techblog", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "source_event_model": "blog_post", "event_model_id": "tech.blog_post", "evidence_policy_ids": ["source_metadata", "article_text"], "event_model_payload": {"headline": "Ask HN: Still Getting [Dead] Posts", "source_name": "Hacker News Best", "source_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50464172", "published_at": "2026-11-12T07:39:52+00:00", "summary": "<p>Unfortunatelly, after quite some time, I'm still getting my posts flagged -- it's a technical blog post on my company's website, flagged as DoA.<p>Still unsure what am I doing wrong, I think the topic is relevant to HN and it's definitely not an ad - the system is a toy experiment to understand how the k8s control-plane works... (but running on a mac)</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50464172\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50464172</a></p>\n<p>Points: 2</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>"}}, "logged_at": "2026-11-12T07:59:04.127755+00:00"}
{"title": "Show HN: Builderoom – find indie-made software by describing what you need", "link": "https://www.builderoom.com/en", "summary": "<p>Hi HN. Builderoom is a site where indie devs, designers and makers list what they build, and you can look for stuff by just describing what you need, like \"physics simulation running in the browser\". Browsing and normal keyword search work without an account.<p>Why I made it: a lot of the time I know what I need but not what the thing is called, so keyword search doesn't help much. And whenever I ship something, every launch site wants the same long form again.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50464162\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50464162</a></p>\n<p>Points: 1</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>", "published": "2026-11-12T07:37:24+00:00", "source": "Hacker News Best", "category": "techblog", "matched_entities": {}, "ontology": {"repo": "BlogRadar", "category": "techblog", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "source_event_model": "blog_post", "event_model_id": "tech.blog_post", "evidence_policy_ids": ["source_metadata", "article_text"], "event_model_payload": {"headline": "Show HN: Builderoom – find indie-made software by describing what you need", "source_name": "Hacker News Best", "source_url": "https://www.builderoom.com/en", "published_at": "2026-11-12T07:37:24+00:00", "summary": "<p>Hi HN. Builderoom is a site where indie devs, designers and makers list what they build, and you can look for stuff by just describing what you need, like \"physics simulation running in the browser\". Browsing and normal keyword search work without an account.<p>Why I made it: a lot of the time I know what I need but not what the thing is called, so keyword search doesn't help much. And whenever I ship something, every launch site wants the same long form again.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50464162\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50464162</a></p>\